-- Hover on a rule written as a list of clauses. Its definition binds the
-- inputs at the GIVEN's own location (L4.Parser.givenInputBinding), so two
-- nodes sit on the GIVEN's name; hover must answer as for any other GIVEN.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour @desc The colour being priced
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE price Red IS 1
DECIDE price c   IS code c

GIVEN x IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE code x IS 3

-- A pattern that is its input's own name compiles to nothing. Hover on it
-- answers with the input's type. An earlier build gave the binding of the
-- later clauses a range from clause 2's body to clause 3's, which covered
-- this pattern, and hover answered NUMBER, the type of that binding.
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE fee Red   IS 1
DECIDE fee Green IS 2
DECIDE fee c     IS 3
